# {{TEAM_NAME}} — SDLC Project Instructions

This repository organizes development work by feature. It is managed with the
[Driver SDLC Plugin (drvr)](https://github.com/driver-ai/driver-sdlc-plugin) in Codex.

## Project structure

```text
{{TEAM_NAME}}/
├── AGENTS.md
├── .mcp.json
├── .gitignore
└── features/
    └── <feature-name>/
        ├── FEATURE_LOG.md
        ├── research/
        ├── plans/
        ├── dry-runs/
        ├── implementation/
        ├── assessment/
        ├── tests/
        └── driver-docs/
```

`FEATURE_LOG.md` is the source of truth for lifecycle state. Plans are the source of truth during
implementation. Use the installed `drvr` skill to create or resume feature work.

## SDLC lifecycle

Features move through Intent, Research, Planning, Validation, Materialization, Implementation,
Review, Bookkeeping, Assessment, Handoff, Pull Request, Verification, and Shipped.

| Phase | drvr workflow |
|---|---|
| Intent | `intent-guidance` |
| Research | `research-guidance` |
| Planning | `planning-guidance` |
| Validation | Ask `drvr` to dry-run the plan |
| Materialization | `materialize-tasks` |
| Implementation | `implementation-guidance` |
| Review and bookkeeping | `sdlc-orchestration` |
| Assessment | Ask `drvr` to assess the feature |
| Handoff | Ask `drvr` to generate handoff docs |
| Pull request | Ask `drvr` to open the PR |

## Key principles

- Separate a pure functional core from the imperative shell. Test the core with values in and
  values out, without mocks. Test the shell against real I/O where practical.
- The user controls decisions and phase transitions.
- Review implementation deviations before bookkeeping.
- Research before building, and implement exactly what the approved plan specifies.
- Commit durable SDLC artifacts with the work they describe.

## Artifact frontmatter

All artifacts use YAML frontmatter with `type`, `status`, `created`, and `updated` fields. Dates use
`YYYY-MM-DD`. Common statuses include `not_started`, `in_progress`, `complete`, `approved`,
`accepted`, `pending_review`, `resolved`, `open`, `confirmed`, and `unverified`.

